# Sources for the Front's press and public role: Fakhreddin Azimi,
# Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953, ch. 5, pp. 250–267;
# Painter and Brew, The Struggle for Iran, ch. 1.
# The recurring press action and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Coordinate the Press
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: public_campaign
view-if: press_coordination_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; press_coordination_timer = 4

= Coordinate the Press

Friendly editors do not take orders from a single
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} press office. They can,
however, agree on which argument should lead the next cycle and which
differences should remain visible rather than becoming contradictory headlines.

Choose the emphasis the secretariat will circulate to editors and speakers.

[? if press_project = "Constitutional editorial network": The cooperating
papers have been leading with representative government and lawful procedure. ?]
[? if press_project = "Oil dossier network": The cooperating papers have been
explaining the disputed oil provisions in detail. ?]
[? if press_project = "Plural editorial compact": The cooperating papers have
been presenting a common demand in several distinct political voices. ?]
[? if press_project = "Fatemi editorial campaign":
{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Fatemi{!</span>!}
has already drawn the friendly editors into a common public campaign. ?]
Editors will judge a new brief against the work their readers have already
seen.

- @press_constitution
- @press_oil
- @press_plural
- @return_card

@press_constitution
title: Lead with constitutional procedure
subtitle: One resource keeps articles returning the dispute to law, cabinet responsibility, and the <span class="term term-parliament">Majles</span>
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource for printing and distribution.
on-arrival: {!
var repeated = Q.press_project === "Constitutional editorial network";
var mature = Q.press_project_stage >= 2;
Q.press_project = "Constitutional editorial network";
Q.press_project_stage += 1;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.press_capacity += mature ? 1 : 4;
Q.constitutional_legitimacy += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.public_mandate += mature ? 0 : 2;
if (repeated && mature) Q.independent_nationalists_dissent += 1;
!}

Editors receive a common brief that connects current demands to representative
institutions and lawful procedure. Their papers retain their own voices, but
readers encounter a recognizable argument across several outlets.

The constitutional case becomes easier to repeat and harder to dismiss as a
momentary slogan. Oil receives less space in this cycle.
[? if press_project_stage > 2: Readers now know this argument well. Repetition
keeps it before them, but wins fewer new adherents and leaves nationalist
editors impatient for a more direct oil case. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@press_oil
title: Explain the oil case term by term
subtitle: One resource lets editors make the concession's disputed terms the center of a common nationalist case
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires one resource for the oil dossier.
on-arrival: {!
var repeated = Q.press_project === "Oil dossier network";
var mature = Q.press_project_stage >= 2;
Q.press_project = "Oil dossier network";
Q.press_project_stage += 1;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.press_capacity += mature ? 1 : 4;
Q.oil_coalition_support += mature ? 1 : 4;
Q.independent_nationalists_relation += mature ? 0 : 2;
if (repeated && mature) Q.iran_party_dissent += 1;
!}

The press brief separates ownership, control, marketing, compensation, and
review instead of asking readers to judge the agreement by one headline
figure.
{!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Independent nationalists{!</span>!} welcome a case that can survive detailed scrutiny.

Editors gain a more disciplined oil vocabulary, and support around national
control grows. Other constitutional issues recede from the immediate campaign.
[? if press_project_stage > 2: The basic distinctions have now been printed
more than once. Another dossier keeps wavering supporters supplied with
arguments, but adds less than the first and frustrates editors who want to
return to constitutional questions. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@press_plural
title: Publish the coalition's disagreements honestly
subtitle: Each component speaks in its own register, making the coalition broader and less uniform
on-arrival: {!
var repeated = Q.press_project === "Plural editorial compact";
var mature = Q.press_project_stage >= 2;
Q.press_project = "Plural editorial compact";
Q.press_project_stage += 1;
Q.press_capacity += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.toilers_dissent -= mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.religious_network_dissent -= mature ? 1 : 3;
if (repeated && mature) Q.public_mandate -= 1;
!}

The secretariat asks friendly papers to identify the common demand while
allowing component organizations to explain their different reasons for
supporting it. Editors report which formulations provoke resistance and which
can travel across constituencies.

{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!} and
{!<span class="term term-religious">!}religious-network{!</span>!} organizers feel less pressure to imitate one
another. The result is credible pluralism, not a single commanding headline.
[? if press_project_stage > 2: The component voices are no longer a novelty.
Another deliberately plural issue reassures insiders, but readers looking for
a decision may hear hesitation instead. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
